Title: Missing break-statement in LL_ADC_DeInit() can cause software to get stuck in a wait-loop

Body:
**Describe the set-up**
 * Nucleo-F031K6
 * STM32CubeIDE 1.15.0 with GCC 12.3 Rel 1

**Describe the bug**
Function LL_ADC_DeInit() contains a wait loop, with timeout detection to make sure the software doesn't hang in case of an unexpected hardware state:

c
  timeout_cpu_cycles = ADC_TIMEOUT_DISABLE_CPU_CYCLES;
  while (LL_ADC_IsDisableOngoing(ADCx) == 1U)
  {
    if(timeout_cpu_cycles-- == 0U)
    {
      /* Time-out error */
      status = ERROR;
    }
  }

The bug is that there is a missing break; statement, in case the timeout occurs. This causes the software to potentially still hang in this loop.

**How To Reproduce**
You can reproduce the problem:

1. Configure and enable the ADC1 on a channel to perform continuous conversions.
2. Call LL_ADC_DeInit(ADC1);

This causes the software to hang, because it is stuck in the before mentioned wait loop.

**Additional context**
Proposed solution: Add the break; statement:

c
  timeout_cpu_cycles = ADC_TIMEOUT_DISABLE_CPU_CYCLES;
  while (LL_ADC_IsDisableOngoing(ADCx) == 1U)
  {
    if(timeout_cpu_cycles-- == 0U)
    {
      /* Time-out error */
      status = ERROR;
      break; /* <<< ADDED */
    }
  }

